## CORE ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLES

### 1. Module Organization (Feature-Based)

```
src/
├── common/              # Shared code (guards, decorators, pipes, filters)
├── auth/                # Authentication & JWT strategy
├── users/               # User management (admin operations)
├── projects/            # Project CRUD
├── contributions/       # Contribution lifecycle
├── rbac/                # Role-based access control & ACL
├── user-projects/       # User-project assignments
├── reviews/             # Review system (placeholder)
├── notifications/       # Notification system
├── audit/               # Audit logging
├── prisma/              # Database module
├── queue/               # Background job processing
├── health/              # Health checks
└── config/              # Configuration & validation
```

**RULES:**
- Each module MUST be self-contained with: module, controller, service, DTOs
- Use barrel exports (`index.ts`) to expose only public API
- NO circular dependencies between modules
- Services > 500 lines MUST be split into sub-services
- Controllers MUST be thin (delegate to services)

### 2. Naming Conventions (STRICT)

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Modules | `{feature}.module.ts` | `users.module.ts` |
| Controllers | `{feature}.controller.ts` | `users.controller.ts` |
| Services | `{feature}.service.ts` | `users.service.ts` |
| DTOs | `{action}-{entity}.dto.ts` | `create-user.dto.ts` |
| Entities | `{entity}.entity.ts` | `user.entity.ts` (Prisma models) |
| Guards | `{name}.guard.ts` | `jwt-auth.guard.ts` |
| Decorators | `{name}.decorator.ts` | `current-user.decorator.ts` |
| Pipes | `{name}.pipe.ts` | `validation.pipe.ts` |
| Filters | `{name}.filter.ts` | `http-exception.filter.ts` |
| Interfaces | `{name}.interface.ts` | `jwt-payload.interface.ts` |
| Events | `{entity}-{action}.event.ts` | `user-approved.event.ts` |
| Listeners | `{entity}-{action}.handler.ts` | `user-email.handler.ts` |

**CRITICAL:** Use kebab-case for file names, PascalCase for class names.

### 3. TypeScript Strict Mode (MANDATORY)

```typescript
// tsconfig.json MUST have:
{
  "strict": true,
  "noImplicitAny": true,
  "strictNullChecks": true,
  "strictFunctionTypes": true,
  "strictBindCallApply": true,
  "strictPropertyInitialization": true,
  "noImplicitThis": true,
  "alwaysStrict": true
}
```

**BANNED:**
- ❌ `any` type (use `unknown` then narrow with type guards)
- ❌ `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error` (fix the type error)
- ❌ Non-null assertion `!` (use optional chaining `?.` or guards)
- ❌ Type assertions with `as` (use type guards instead)

**REQUIRED:**
- ✅ Explicit return types on all functions
- ✅ Explicit types for all function parameters
- ✅ Use `readonly` for immutable properties
- ✅ Use `const` over `let` (enforce with ESLint)

