## BACKGROUND JOBS (pg-boss 10.4.x)

### 1. Queue Service (Manual Wiring Pattern)

```typescript
// Enqueue job (in service)
await this.pgBossService.getBoss().send('send-email', {
  to: user.email,
  subject: 'Welcome',
  body: 'Hello',
}, {
  retryLimit: 3,
  retryDelay: 60,        // seconds
  retryBackoff: true,    // exponential backoff
  expireInSeconds: 3600, // job expires after 1 hour
});

// Process job (in processor)
@Injectable()
export class EmailProcessor implements OnModuleInit, OnModuleDestroy {
  private workerStopFunctions: Array<() => Promise<void>> = [];

  constructor(private readonly pgBossService: PgBossService) {}

  async onModuleInit(): Promise<void> {
    const boss = this.pgBossService.getBoss();
    
    // Register worker and store stop function for cleanup
    const stopFunction = await boss.work<EmailJobData>('send-email', async (job) => {
      await this.emailService.send(job.data);
    });
    
    this.workerStopFunctions.push(stopFunction);
  }

  async onModuleDestroy(): Promise<void> {
    // Gracefully stop all workers
    await Promise.all(
      this.workerStopFunctions.map(stop => stop())
    );
  }
}
```

**CRITICAL:**
- `@OnWorkerEvent` decorator DOES NOT EXIST in pg-boss
- Use manual `boss.work()` registration in `onModuleInit()`
- ALWAYS store stop functions and call them in `onModuleDestroy()`
- Workers receive a SINGLE job object, not an array

**RULES:**
- Use queue for: emails, notifications, heavy computations
- Job names MUST be kebab-case: `send-email`, `generate-report`
- Job data MUST be serializable (no functions, classes)
- ALWAYS set retry policy with ALL options:
  - `retryLimit: 3` (number of retries)
  - `retryDelay: 60` (seconds between retries)
  - `retryBackoff: true` (exponential backoff)
  - `expireInSeconds: 3600` (job expiry to prevent stale jobs)
- ALWAYS implement graceful shutdown with `onModuleDestroy()`

